Falsifies `e1000e::proofs::one_receive_examines_at_most_one_lap_of_the_ring`.

The defect: the receive loop loses its per-call limit and runs until a descriptor reads as not yet
written or a frame is delivered. A device that writes each descriptor again as soon as it is handed
back, with a frame that is not delivered, then keeps one call examining descriptors without end.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!` on the count of status words read, at the seventeenth read.

